<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Penoles gives metals sales vols.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Penoles gives metals sales vols.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Industrias Penoles, the world's largest refined silver producer, detailed on Tuesday sales volumes of precious and base metals in the first quarter of 1997. Precious metals in kg, base metals in tonnes.</p>
<p>    Metal	   Q197	   Q196	  Q496</p>
<p>    Gold	    2,407	  1,970	  2,415</p>
<p>    Silver	445,990	383,684	487,247</p>
<p>	Domestic  102,560	101,920	101,055</p>
<p>	Exports   343,430	281,764	386,192</p>
<p>    Lead	   43,024	 30,628	 46,039</p>
<p>	Domestic   23,220	 16,121	 23,095</p>
<p>	Exports    19,804	 14,507	 22,939</p>
<p>    Zinc	   30,713	 26,183	 29,421</p>
<p>	Domestic   19,329	 16,121	 16,170</p>
<p>	Exports    11,384	 11,428	 12,672</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530))</p>
<p>E-mail at chris.aspin@reuters.com</p>
